DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbhhyyvveeccttll command is a control utility for active bhyve(8) virtual ma‐
     chine instances.

     _N_o_t_e: Most bbhhyyvveeccttll flags are intended for querying and setting the state
     of an active instance.  These commands are intended for development pur‐
     poses, and are not documented here.  A complete list can be obtained by
     executing bbhhyyvveeccttll without any arguments.

     The user-facing options are as follows:

     ----vvmm==_<_v_m_n_a_m_e_>
                  Operate on the virtual machine _<_v_m_n_a_m_e_>.

     ----ccrreeaattee     Create the specified VM.

     ----ddeessttrrooyy    Destroy the specified VM.

     ----ggeett--ssttaattss  Retrieve statistics for the specified VM.

     ----iinnjjeecctt--nnmmii
                  Inject a non-maskable interrupt (NMI) into the VM.

     ----ffoorrccee--rreesseett
                  Force the VM to reset.

     ----ffoorrccee--ppoowweerrooffff
                  Force the VM to power off.

     ----cchheecckkppooiinntt==_<_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e_>
                  Save a snapshot of a virtual machine.  The guest memory con‐
                  tents are saved in the file given in _<_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e_>.  The guest
                  device and vCPU state are saved in the file _<_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e_>_._k_e_r_n.

     ----ssuussppeenndd==_<_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e_>
                  Save a snapshot of a virtual machine similar to
                  ----cchheecckkppooiinntt.  The virtual machine will terminate after the
                  snapshot has been saved.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The bbhhyyvveeccttll utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Destroy the VM called fbsd10:

           bhyvectl --vm=fbsd10 --destroy

CCOOMMPPAATTIIBBIILLIITTYY
